{{Clear}}

''Italicised oblasts were only partially under [[2014 pro-Russian unrest in Ukraine|Ukrainian government control]], and voting took place only in areas where it could be organised. No voting was held in [[Autonomous Republic of Crimea|Crimea]] or [[Sevastopol]] following their [[2014 Russian annexation of Crimea|annexation by Russia]].''

==Reactions==
Despite [[2014 Ukrainian presidential election#Russian reaction|Russia's earlier protest at rescheduling the election]] and the general tense relation between the countries at the time because of the [[Annexation of Crimea by the Russian Federation|annexation of Crimea]] and the [[Russian military intervention in Ukraine (2014–present)|Russian military intervention in Ukraine]], [[Russian president]] [[Vladimir Putin]] recognised the vote.<ref name="VP recognise">{{cite web | url=https://blogs.wsj.com/washwire/2014/05/26/u-s-lauds-ukraine-election-amid-hopes-for-easing-standoff/ | title=U.S. Lauds Ukraine Election Amid Hopes for Easing Standoff | work=The Wall Street Journal | date=26 May 2014| access-date=27 May 2014| author=Talley, Ian}}</ref>

The leaders of the [[self-proclaimed]] [[Donetsk People's Republic]] and [[Luhansk People's Republic]], controlling large parts of the [[Donbas]] region of [[Eastern Ukraine]], declared that the regions had made their choice shown in the [[Sham election|highly disputed]] results of the [[2014 Donbas status referendums|status referendum]] of 11 May.<ref name="HP"/>

[[US president]] [[Barack Obama]] congratulated Petro Poroshenko with his victory by telephone 2 days after the election.<ref>[https://online.wsj.com/news/articles/SB10001424052702304811904579588171670090480 Obama Calls Ukrainian President-Elect Poroshenko With Congratulations], [[The Wall Street Journal]] (27 May 2014)</ref> This was also done by [[President of the European Commission]] [[José Manuel Barroso]] and [[President of the European Parliament|European Parliament President]] [[Martin Schulz]] and other [[EU]] leaders such as [[German chancellor]] [[Angela Merkel]] and [[French president]] [[François Hollande]].<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20140808050409/http://enpi-info.eu/maineast.php?id=37402&id_type=1&lang_id=450 Ukraine: EU leaders congratulate Poroshenko and praise elections held against the odds] [[European Union Association Agreement|ENPI Info Centre]] (27 May 2014)</ref><ref>[http://www.kyivpost.com/content/ukraine-abroad/wall-street-journal-merkel-congratulates-ukraines-poroshenko-on-election-win-349628.html Wall Street Journal: Merkel congratulates Ukraine's Poroshenko on election win], [[Kyiv Post]] (27 May 2014)</ref>

